{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509789-need-help-to-introduce-mage","id":1509789,"title":"Need help to introduce Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-26T15:26:09-07:00","id":1509789,"title":"Need help to introduce Mage","content":"I'm planning to create a mage antagonist, problem is that i don't have the core book of MTA so the only one thing i can use at the moment is their description in my WTA book and some description found on google.<br /> I've found the 9 spheres, i've learn how paradox work (at least i think i understand), but in read somewhere that those sphere can disapear with time and new can appear.<br /> How do you handle sphere and their use? Do you create your own sphere for your npc's and how do you chose the concept?<br /> <br /> Paradox is described as the &quot;price&quot; for &quot;bad&quot; use of true magic, but from what i know it depend on what HUMANS think possible or not. In WTA humans are living being among other, their intelligence being an addition diverted by the wyrm, how to make paradox work without that human influence?<br /> <br /> Finally mage can spend many round to get the amount of success they need, is it something you would let you Werewolf (or Vampire) pc's do when they need a specific effect from their own powers (troll skin, luna's armor, persuasion, bury the wolf...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 04-26-2023, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T15:31:43-07:00","id":1509790,"title":"","content":"I have a suggestion. Ignore Mage. Have a Wizard and let it do whatever your plot needs. It's not like he needs to have player facing stats anyway. He can do exactly what he needs to do to be a threat. Everything else is just unnecessary overhead for yourself (and the game of Werewolf you're trying to run).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T16:10:54-07:00","id":1509793,"title":"","content":"Yeah, learning another game just for an antagonist NPC isn't worth it; esp. not a game that can be as difficult to grok as Mage. There's a reason the books have loose stats for the other types in their books instead of expecting you to go and get the other games just for some odd antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T01:04:57-07:00","id":1509847,"title":"","content":"I'd give mages as stated in ascention a miss as well aside from the fact they're genrally considered op vs werewolves they're also a lot to handle.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep your rules tight rather than winging it I'd recommend either using sorcerer rules and/or picking some appropriately sorcerous gifts. Then just Paradox if they botch a spell<br /> <br /> To answer your questions.<br /> <br /> I've never heard of spheres disappearing. <br /> <br /> Witnesses to Paradox are what's called sleepers a sleeper is an ordinary human who ascribes to conventionalish ideas and isn't 'awoken' to the truths of reality. In terms of wyrm subversion it probably depends on depth, a call centre rep at a pentex company is almost certainly still a sleeper but a fomori isn't.<br /> <br /> No, thats a perk of being a mage. Much like healing any bashing instantly is a perk of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-27-2023, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T02:39:06-07:00","id":1509849,"title":"","content":"Ignoring the mage rules seems indeed easier for an antagonist, i needed some informations because that antagonist is supposed to be hunt by the party and by other mage wich could become temporary allies of the party (if the pc's want to according to their character)<br /> <br /> With the possibility of allies mage i thought some basic informations about how their magic work would be useful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T03:51:51-07:00","id":1509854,"title":"","content":"So, the thing about mages, is that the possibilities are technically endless. When a Garou learns a new Gift or Rite, or attunes a new Fetish, they get singular package that work how it works. When a mage increases a Sphere, they get a infinitely large set of new things they can do: both in expanding the power over the subjects of the Sphere, and combining this new power with their other Spheres in new and different ways.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing about learning Mage is not really &quot;what can a mage do?&quot; but rather, &quot;why can't this mage do this thing?&quot; In Mage, mages are literally willing reality to change into what they want it to be (if usually temporarily). What holds them back is that the universe is far too complex to just will it into shape solely with the knowledge that reality can be shaped in the first place. To shape reality mages need a way to understand reality and give themselves a scaffold their still human minds can use to frame what they're doing. This overarching philosophy is called a Focus (in M20 anyway): a set of beliefs in how magic works (paradigm), the way beliefs can be used to manifest changes (practices), and the specific methods to enact it (instruments).<br /> <br /> This Focus is necessary to let mages know what they're doing, but also limits them because what they do has to fit into that Focus to work. A mage that believes their magic is enabled by praying for permission to a higher power to alter how that power made the world can't just build a wand that shoots lightning bolt when you say the activation word. If they want a magic item of burning things, it has to fit their religious style.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sphere's are simply a measure of which parts of reality a mage knows how to manipulate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T10:46:29-07:00","id":1509872,"title":"","content":"My first impression was that sphere was a part of universe a mage can interact with, so you say the mage power is to change reality and sphere are just what they understand about a particular part of reality<br /> <br /> what i cannot understand is what's the sleepers role in that? If mage can manipulate reality how does sleepers can be an obstacle? Do they act as some kind of... witnesses? But why humans? If their beliefs define what's possible or not to do for a mage it give them a pretty big role in universe balance, no?<br /> Maybe my point of view isn't right because i see thing from WTA sight but i don't like the fact to give humans so much importance in the universe, they're not the only intelligent beings, there's spirits (far more intelligent for some), they're not the most important life form for the life balance on earth (only it's most dangerous ennemy)<br /> <br /> To get back on the subject the 9 sphere represent what mages can manipulate, but can there be more or those 9 are enough to manipulate every aspect of reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T11:35:25-07:00","id":1509874,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sleepers&quot; is a word that's complicated by having mechanical and in-character definitions that are not always 100% aligned. But the essential thing is that all &quot;humans&quot; are mages waiting to &quot;wake up.&quot; So every human (or at least every human that still has their magical potential intact) is subconsciously shaping reality too. In modern times this is called Consensus: the collective subconscious effect of Sleepers defining a mutual reality. So, basically, Sleepers are inadvertently casting countermagic at any magic that violates Consensus. The only way for their innate magical potential to express itself is to help reinforce Consensus (or the local rules of Reality in places that Consensus doesn't dominate).<br /> <br /> This also metaphysically explains why non-mages don't suffer from Sleepers witnessing their powers: mages need to be Awakened to learn Spheres and understand reality well enough to try to counter powers that aren't reality warping mage-magic.<br /> <br /> The effect of Sleepers is also very weak once you leave Earth (either physically go into space, or go to the Umbra). If you drag a Sleeper into the Umbra, they have no inherent effect on mages in the Umbra with them, because the Umbra is too strongly controlled by vaster entities than one mere human's latent magical potential. Umbra exploring mages have to contend with the rules of Realms like any other Umbra explorer does. So Sleepers impact on the whole universe isn't so grand.<br /> <br /> Mage also has a concept called the Earthly Foundations: axiomatic truths so strong that even mages can't change them. Mages cannot create a rock so heavy they can't lift it, effectively, is the rule of the Mage metaphysics. Of course, who created the Earthly Foundations - since magic itself is impossible without them - is not known. Gaia and the Triat are, however, a great set of candidates for a WtA game. <br /> <br /> The number of Spheres is currently nine because both the Traditions and the Technocracy spend centuries coding that into Consensus. So, in theory, it can be changed. In the past there were different numbers of them, and in the present variations have become more commonplace. So nine is not an Earthly Foundation. It's not an immutable rule. But it's a strong enough rule that breaking out of it would be extremely difficult. However, whatever the number is, it's always dividing up everything in the universe. In the Dark Ages most mages studied four Pillars (which were all different based on magical Fellowship), and those Pillars covered the same things as the nine Spheres... just arranged differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T11:59:54-07:00","id":1509875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what i cannot understand is what's the sleepers role in that? If mage can manipulate reality how does sleepers can be an obstacle? Do they act as some kind of... witnesses? But why humans? If their beliefs define what's possible or not to do for a mage it give them a pretty big role in universe balance, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Mage gives humans a big role. As for the most average &amp; simple explanation: Mage posits that all humans are mages in potence. They're &quot;sleepers&quot; because they have a sleeping Avatar (the source of magick) can &quot;awake&quot; (making them into mages). And their latent power acts in a way that can conflitct with other mages. The rabbit hole goes beyond that, but I don't think you need to go there because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe my point of view isn't right because i see thing from WTA sight but i don't like the fact to give humans so much importance in the universe, they're not the only intelligent beings, there's spirits (far more intelligent for some), they're not the most important life form for the life balance on earth (only it's most dangerous ennemy) </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. That whole thing may conflict with Werewolf at some points.<br /> <br /> So, scrap it. it's not like the deep lore of another game needs to be taken in count to that point.<br /> <br /> Something many Werewolf books do when crossovering it's to say that the Weaver it's the force behind Paradox (in the Book of the Weaver a Paradox Spirit it's even included under her brood). It happens when mages do outlandish things because the Weaver doesn't like her reality changing.<br /> As per the human effect, well, you may house-rule they don't matter. OR maybe, as a species specially &quot;blessed&quot; by the Weaver they DO matter - because humans <i>are special </i>in Werewolf in that specific sense (they have gifts from Science's big spirit-thing, and two big Weaver spirits more, no?, my memory it's a quite foggy on that). &quot;Human make reality more weaver-y&quot;, doesn't seem that out of the place considering the effects cities and such have on the Umbrascape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To get back on the subject the 9 sphere represent what mages can manipulate, but can there be more or those 9 are enough to manipulate every aspect of reality? </div> </div> </div>They're quite enough.<br /> <br /> Getting deeper into this isn't something you will need, but to give a glimpse of what a more complex answer would entail: There are optional rules for Mage that include &quot;lesser&quot; Spheres (that are more specific but don't add anything new). Some suplements add Technocratic Spheres (that <i>replace</i> one of the nine with a similar Sphere with sligthly different mechanics). Dark age had Pillars as what existed before Spheres - quite the can of worms. Or, for the Lore enthusiasts, the fabled 10th, that nobody knows what may do because nobody has it, and may not even exist.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2023, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T16:45:58-07:00","id":1509907,"title":"","content":"&quot;Lesser sphere&quot;? Do you mean something like &quot;fire sphere&quot; technology sphere&quot; or any more specific concept like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T17:34:20-07:00","id":1509910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509789-need-help-to-introduce-mage?p=1509907#post1509907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lesser sphere&quot;? Do you mean something like &quot;fire sphere&quot; technology sphere&quot; or any more specific concept like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember the terminology, but you got the gist of it. It has to be an aspect of the world that's much too concrete to be a whole Sphere.<br /> <br /> Fire it's used as an example. So, yeah.<br /> <br /> Technology, on the other hand. I don't think so ... Think that there's a whole faction that sees all the 9 Spheres under the guise of science &amp; technology. Unless it's a<i> very specific</i> field of technology (say, the Sphere of &quot;Botanics&quot;), or a very limiting interpretation of what &quot;technology&quot; <i>IS</i> (like a Sphere of &quot;machines&quot; - and I don't want to hear even a <i>joke</i> about &quot;the human body it's a biological machine&quot; or something like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I would say no<br /> <br /> It's an optional rule I never used, and, frankly, wouldn't recommend to use. Unless you absolutely want a mage whose magick it's <i>dynamic</i>, yet very gimmicky to the point it's actually a problem, mechanically. Seting such boundaries it's an extra workload that a <i>Mage </i>ST doesn't need, when you can probably represent the same character with the vanilla rules and a clever use of Focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2023, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}